{"raw": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/3764967/adjunct-faculty-various-disciplines-midland-mi": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, Various Disciplines, Midland, MI", "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Various Disciplines, Midland, MI Location Midland, MI Job Type Adjunct Faculty Job Number 03232 Division Midland Campus Department UG Academic Admin and Support Opening Date 10/16/2022 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University seeks a dynamic individual with a strong record of teaching at the undergraduate level, industry experience, and strong interpersonal skills to teach at the Midland, Michigan campus. The candidate would be expected to teach some daytime classes with the possibility of teaching either day or evening classes in the future. Northwood University offers the Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA) degree. The need for adjunct faculty is based on student enrollment and varies by semester. Desired disciplines include: Accounting Automotive Marketing and Management Automotive Aftermarket Management Business Law Computer Science Cybersecurity Data Analytics Digital Marketing Economics Entrepreneurship Environmental Science Finance Health Care Management Hospitality Management History Humanities International Business Management Management Information Systems Marketing Marketing Communications Merchandising & Marketing Mathematics Operations & Supply Chain Management Political Science Speech Sport Management & Esports Management Sustainability Management Qualifications Required Qualifications: \u2022 Master\u2019s degree from a regionally-accredited institution or a Master's degree in a closely-related discipline with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in specific discipline \u2022 Experience teaching undergraduate courses in discipline or closely related disciplines \u2022 For business-related disciplines, industry experience closely related to the discipline \u2022 Ability to interact effectively with a wide and diverse range of students and colleagues \u2022 Well-developed oral and written communication skills in a variety of delivery formats Desired Qualifications: \u2022 Experience teaching both face to face and online undergraduate courses Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. ABOUT NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. Participation in 403b retirement program for eligible employees; sick leave, tuition benefit discounts for eligible employees; access to employee assistance program; wellness benefits; access to other employee discount programs. Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5477986/assistant-professor-accounting": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Accounting", "description": "Assistant Professor, Accounting Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03461 Division Midland Campus Department Accounting Department Opening Date 09/10/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University seeks a dynamic individual with strong interpersonal skills, significant industry experience, and a strong record of teaching at the undergraduate level to begin teaching in the Spring 2027 semester at our Midland, Michigan campus. The candidate will be hired with the rank of Assistant Professor. Responsibilities Northwood University is a teaching-focused university with HLC and ACBSP accreditation offering undergraduate and graduate degrees in business-related disciplines. The teaching load for full-time undergraduate faculty is 30 credit hours per academic year (Fall and Spring semesters). Candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in Accounting. Additional responsibilities and expectations may include participation in on-going curriculum planning and review; internship and/or practicum supervision; research and scholarly activities; professional/instructional development; university committee activities; recruitment and retention activities; and other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Master's degree in Accounting or closely related field from an accredited institution. Significant industry experience in accounting or closely related field Experience training and/or teaching accounting or related disciplines. Ability to interact effectively with a wide and diverse range of students and colleagues. Well-developed oral and written communication skills in a variety of delivery formats. Preferred: Earned Doctorate or terminal degree from accredited institution (such as J.D., Ph.D., OBA; ABD candidates considered if completion date is within one year of hire). Experience teaching undergraduate courses. Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5138122/assistant-professor-aftermarket-management": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Aftermarket Management", "description": "Assistant Professor, Aftermarket Management Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03424 Division Midland Campus Department Automotive Aftermarket Opening Date 11/10/2025 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University seeks a dynamic individual with strong interpersonal skills, significant industry experience and a strong record of teaching at the undergraduate level to begin teaching in the Spring 2027 semester at our Midland, Michigan campus. The candidate will be hired with the rank of assistant professor. Responsibilities Northwood University is a teaching-focused university with HLC and ACBSP accreditation offering undergraduate and graduate degrees in business-related disciplines. The teaching load for full-time undergraduate faculty is30 credit hours per academic year (Fall and Spring semesters).Candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in Automotive Aftermarket Management, Management, and/or Marketing. Additional responsibilities and expectations may include participation in on-going curriculum planning and review; internship and/or practicum supervision; research and scholarly activities; professional/instructional development; service as department chair and program quality lead; university committee activities; recruitment and retention activities; and other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Master\u2019s degree in a business-related discipline. Five or more years of experience directly related to the Automotive Aftermarket Industry Experience training and/or teaching. Preferred: Earned Doctorate or terminal degree from accredited institution (such as J.D., Ph.D., OBA; ABD candidates considered if completion date is within one year of hire) Experience teaching undergraduate courses Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. ABOUT NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5486314/assistant-professor-entrepreneurship": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Entrepreneurship", "description": "Assistant Professor, Entrepreneurship Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03506 Division Midland Campus Department Entrepreneurship Department Opening Date 09/17/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University seeks a dynamic individual with strong interpersonal skills, significant industry experience, and a strong record of teaching at the undergraduate level to begin teaching in the Spring 2027 semester at our Midland, Michigan campus. The candidate will be hired with the rank of Assistant Professor. Responsibilities Northwood University is a teaching-focused university with HLC and ACBSP accreditation offering undergraduate and graduate degrees in business-related disciplines. The teaching load for full-time undergraduate faculty is 30 credit hours per academic year (Fall and Spring semesters). Candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate courses within the Entrepreneurship program. Additional responsibilities and expectations may include participation in on-going curriculum planning and review; internship and/or practicum supervision; research and scholarly activities; professional/instructional development; university committee activities; recruitment and retention activities; and other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Master's degree in Entrepreneurship or closely related field from an accredited institution. Significant industry experience in entrepreneurial endeavors Experience training and/or teaching in management and entrepreneurship disciplines. Ability to interact effectively with a wide and diverse range of students and colleagues. Well-developed oral and written communication skills in a variety of delivery formats. Preferred: Earned doctorate or terminal degree from accredited institution (such as J.D., Ph.D., OBA; ABD candidates considered if completion date is within one year of hire). Experience teaching undergraduate courses. Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/4886132/assistant-professor-management": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Management", "description": "Assistant Professor, Management Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03399 Division Midland Campus Department Management Department Opening Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University seeks a dynamic individual with strong interpersonal skills, significant industry experience and a strong record of teaching at the undergraduate level to begin teaching in the Spring 2027 semester at our Midland, Michigan campus. The candidate will be hired with the rank of assistant professor. Responsibilities Northwood University is a teaching-focused university with HLC and ACBSP accreditation offering undergraduate and graduate degrees in business-related disciplines. The teaching load for full-time undergraduate faculty is30 credit hours per academic year (Fall and Spring semesters). Candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in Management, Leadership, International Business, and Entrepreneurship. Additional responsibilities and expectations may include participation in on-going curriculum planning and review; internship and/or practicum supervision; research and scholarly activities; professional/instructional development; university committee activities; recruitment and retention activities; and other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Master's degree in Management, Entrepreneurship or closely related field from an accredited institution. Significant industry experience in managerial or leadership roles and entrepreneurial Experience in training and/or teaching in management and entrepreneurship disciplines. Ability to interact effectively with a wide and diverse range of students and colleagues. Well-developed oral and written communication skills in a variety of delivery formats. Preferred: Earned Doctorate or terminal degree from accredited institution (such as J.D., Ph.D., OBA; ABD candidates considered if completion date is within one year of hire). Experience teaching undergraduate courses. Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5486539/assistant-professor-mathematics": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Mathematics", "description": "Assistant Professor, Mathematics Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03505 Division Midland Campus Department Math/Science Department Opening Date 09/17/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University seeks a dynamic individual with strong interpersonal skills, significant industry experience, and a strong record of teaching at the undergraduate level to begin teaching in the Spring 2027 semester at our Midland, Michigan campus. The candidate will be hired with the rank of Assistant Professor. Responsibilities Northwood University is a teaching-focused university with HLC and ACBSP accreditation offering undergraduate and graduate degrees in business-related disciplines. The teaching load for full-time undergraduate faculty is 30 credit hours per academic year (Fall and Spring semesters). Candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate courses within the Mathematics program. Additional responsibilities and expectations may include participation in on-going curriculum planning and review; internship and/or practicum supervision; research and scholarly activities; professional/instructional development; university committee activities; recruitment and retention activities; and other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Master's degree in Mathematics or closely related field from an accredited institution. Significant industry experience in a mathematics-related position. Experience training and/or teaching in mathematics. Ability to interact effectively with a wide and diverse range of students and colleagues. Well-developed oral and written communication skills in a variety of delivery formats. Preferred: Earned doctorate or terminal degree from accredited institution (such as J.D., Ph.D., OBA; ABD candidates considered if completion date is within one year of hire). Experience teaching undergraduate courses. Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5356316/assistant-track-and-field-cross-country-coach": {"title": "Assistant Track and Field/Cross Country Coach", "description": "Assistant Track and Field/Cross Country Coach Location Midland, MI Job Type Part-Time Job Number 03471 Division Midland Campus Department Track & Cross Country, Men's Opening Date 05/27/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University is currently seeking applications for the part-time position of Men's and Women's Track and Field/Cross Country Assistant Coach. Responsibilities The coach will coordinate all activities related to running the program including: recruiting practices games scheduling budget management, etc. Will work closely with the coaching staff and especially the cross country, sprints, jumps and multis student athletes. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred. Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. ABOUT NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. Participation in 403b retirement program for eligible employees; sick leave, tuition benefit discounts for eligible employees; access to employee assistance program; wellness benefits; access to other employee discount programs. Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/4107612/asst-professor-on-ground-online-devos-grad-school-multiple-disciplines-in-bus": {"title": "Asst Professor (on-ground/online), DeVos Grad School, Multiple Disciplines in Business - Finance/AI", "description": "Asst Professor (on-ground/online), DeVos Grad School, Multiple Disciplines in Business - Finance/AI Location Richard DeVos Graduate School of Management, Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03274 Division Graduate School Department Graduate Faculty Opening Date 07/07/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University\u2019s DeVos Graduate School of Management has an immediate need for qualified faculty to teach in our DBA, MBA and MS programs. This position will have classes on the Midland, MI campus as well as online. The candidate should hold a terminal degree in Finance with teaching and integrating AI in the classroom.The ideal candidate will have demonstrated an ability to teach in both on-ground and online modalities including discussion-based classroom meetings during the day and evening. Willingness to embrace our unique problem-based pedagogy is essential to achieve the transformational competencies that DeVos Graduate School students accomplish during and as a result of their program. Faculty members also serve as Dissertation Committee Members and Chairs and must have a commitment to the long-term success of our students. Responsibilities The candidate hired in this position will be a key member of our faculty and should be comfortable in representing the graduate school and our programming to internal and external constituents. Full-time faculty members have a role in advising, admissions, assessment and mentoring adjunct faculty. Qualifications A Ph.D. or DBA in a business-related discipline from a regionally accredited institution with substantive academic or professional experience in: Finance Artificial Intelligence Analytics Experience serving as DBA/PhD Dissertation Committee chair and/or committee member. Experience designing, developing and implementing graduate level courses. An understanding of LMS systems, especially Blackboard Ultra. Preference is given to those who have extensive real-world business experience as well as the relevant degree. Candidates must also be comfortable facilitating problem-based learning and learner-center classrooms. Expectations Application Information To be considered, applicants must provide the following: A completed online application A cover letter explaining what locations and areas of instruction are of interest. An unofficial transcript attached to the application. Incomplete applications or applications without the appropriate academic credentials will not be considered. If offered employment, an official transcript will be required. The DeVos Graduate School is part of the Northwood University system and is an established and highly regarded institution of graduate education in business. Further information about the Graduate School philosophy, programs and approach can be found at https://www.northwood.edu/graduate Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5515681/athletic-pep-band-director": {"title": "Athletic Pep Band Director", "description": "Athletic Pep Band Director Location Midland, MI Job Type Part-Time Job Number 03507 Division Midland Campus Department Emerging Sports Opening Date 10/14/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Athletic Pep Band Director Responsibilities Supervision and development of band members Recruitment event and practice preparation and management provide pep band at as many on-campus events as possible with focus on athletic events (pep rallies, football games, volleyball matches, basketball games as well as directed hockey, lacrosse and soccer match-ups) community and alumni relations as assigned making travel arrangements if necessary drive to and from events and practices (as needed) administrative duties as assigned fund-raising as assigned Other duties as assigned by Sr. Associate AD for Emerging Sports Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree Working knowledge of music and instrumental instruction Previous directing experience Expectations Adhere to Northwood University rules, regulations, and policies Adhere to institutional regulations and policies Provide leadership to promote a life-changing, positive experience for your band members Promote academic success in the classroom and members being a positive presence on campus Have success on the court while representing Northwood with class and integrity Meet and exceed squad size numbers to aid our admissions department Assist in specific community service projects for each team to learn the importance of giving back to the community Represent Northwood in a professional, positive manner in the office, on-campus and in the community Be flexible Be a good team player within the department Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ Participation in 403b retirement program for eligible employees; sick leave, tuition benefit discounts for eligible employees; access to employee assistance program; wellness benefits; access to other employee discount programs. Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5356001/crm-administrator": {"title": "CRM Administrator", "description": "CRM Administrator Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03475 Division Advancement, Marketing & Communications Department Communications Opening Date 09/14/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University, America's Free-Enterprise University, is seeking a CRM Administrator to provide leadership, technical expertise, and day-to-day administration of Slate in support of enrollment, recruitment, admissions, and engagement goals. As part of a distinctive, mission-driven community that develops free-enterprise leaders, this role will help strengthen the digital systems and experiences that connect prospective students, current students, and University partners with Northwood. The CRM Administrator is responsible for optimizing CRM performance, managing user access and system configuration, developing workflows, queries, reports, dashboards, and communication tools, and ensuring accurate data flow across Slate, Colleague, and other enterprise systems. The position will also identify opportunities to use automation and AI-enabled tools to improve efficiency, communication, reporting, and decision-making. Through training, documentation, troubleshooting, and responsive support, the CRM Administrator will help strengthen CRM adoption and effective Slate use across the University. Work Arrangemen t Remote work may be available for the right candidate. This position requires the flexibility to be on campus in Midland, Michigan, periodically and as business needs require, including for key University initiatives, partner engagements, team collaboration, training, and Slate-focused events or summits. Responsibilities Oversee Slate daily operations, system performance, configuration, and ongoing optimization. Serve as the primary administrator for Slate, including user access, profiles, roles, permissions, and routine system administration. Translate business needs into CRM solutions by developing workflows, queries, reports, and process improvements that support recruitment, admissions, and engagement. Build and maintain dashboards that provide clear visibility into enrollment funnel activity, performance trends, and conversion opportunities. Manage CRM-based communication tools, including email and SMS campaigns, to support timely and effective outreach. Coordinate CRM integrations with Colleague, the website, marketing platforms, and other enterprise systems to promote accurate, consistent data flow. Lead CRM-related projects by defining priorities, tracking milestones, monitoring system activity, and ensuring timely completion of deliverables. Partner with Enrollment, Marketing, IT, and other stakeholders to align CRM initiatives with institutional priorities. Identify opportunities to use automation and AI-enabled tools to improve CRM efficiency, communication, reporting, and decision-making. Provide training, documentation, and responsive support to strengthen user adoption and effective Slate use across the institution. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in a related field required; master\u2019s preferred. 3-5+ years of experience with CRM/ERP systems, preferably Slate and Colleague, in higher education. Working knowledge of AI tools and their application in operations and automation. Experience building CRM queries, reports, dashboards, workflows, and communication campaigns. Knowledge of enrollment management, admissions operations, recruitment funnels, or student lifecycle processes. Ability to translate business needs into technical CRM requirements and practical user solutions. Understanding of data privacy, security, and compliance expectations related to student records. Experience with data integration, system interoperability, and managing data across multiple platforms. Ability to provide effective, quality service to our internal and external customers. Strong project management and organizational skills. Expectations Communicates effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. Participates in periodic on-campus obligations and key in-person engagements to support collaboration, training, partner relationships, and University priorities. Manages multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Applies a continuous improvement mindset focused on efficiency and outcomes. Maintains high standards for data integrity, privacy, security, and responsible use of student information. Demonstrates a service-oriented approach to supporting users, resolving issues, and strengthening CRM adoption. Connects CRM strategy and functionality to enrollment goals, digital experience, and institutional priorities. Documents processes, configurations, workflows, and system changes to support consistency, continuity, and training. Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. ABOUT NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5497206/digital-experience-web-strategy-manager": {"title": "Digital Experience & Web Strategy Manager", "description": "Digital Experience & Web Strategy Manager Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03498 Division Advancement, Marketing & Communications Department Marketing Opening Date 09/28/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Position Summary Northwood University seeks a Digital Experience & Web Strategy Manager to lead and manage the strategy, performance and continued development of the digital platforms that shape how prospective students discover, evaluate and engage with the University. This role is responsible for creating a high-performing, accessible and data-informed web experience that supports enrollment and institutional growth. Working at the intersection of web strategy, user experience, content, analytics, systems integration and emerging technology, the manager will help advance Northwood\u2019s development as a modern, digitally integrated university. The successful candidate will bring a product and platform mindset to the University\u2019s digital ecosystem, connecting audience needs with institutional priorities and measurable outcomes. Responsibilities Web Strategy and Platform Management Lead the strategy, structure and ongoing optimization of Northwood\u2019s web ecosystem. Manage information architecture, navigation, page structure and interaction design. Evaluate website performance and recommend improvements based on user behavior, institutional priorities and industry standards. Identify and reduce friction across key user journeys, particularly those related to student recruitment and enrollment. Partner with content owners, designers, developers and other stakeholders to maintain a consistent and effective digital experience. Ensure web experiences meet accessibility, usability, responsive design and performance standards. Content Strategy and Management Write, edit and update website content to ensure it remains accurate, timely and relevant. Adapt content for prospective students, parents, current students, alumni, industry partners and other key audiences. Translate complex academic and institutional information into clear, engaging and user-friendly language. Use audience needs, search behavior, analytics and enrollment priorities to guide content decisions. Partner with subject-matter experts and content owners to verify information and maintain accuracy. Establish processes for routine content review, governance and the removal of outdated information. Ensure digital content reflects Northwood\u2019s brand, voice, accessibility standards and strategic priorities. User Experience and Conversion Optimization Develop user-centered digital experiences that help prospective students find information and take meaningful next steps. Map and evaluate digital journeys across inquiry, application, admission and enrollment. Improve calls to action, forms, landing pages and conversion pathways. Use testing, behavioral data and user feedback to guide improvements. Establish performance measures and report on the impact of digital experience initiatives. Analytics and Performance Insights Analyze user behavior across the website and other digital touchpoints. Translate analytics into practical recommendations and system-level improvements. Develop dashboards and reporting that connect digital activity with recruitment and enrollment outcomes. Monitor conversion performance, engagement patterns, search behavior and emerging trends. Promote consistent measurement practices and data-informed decision-making. Digital Ecosystem Integration Help connect the University\u2019s website, CRM and engagement platforms into a unified digital experience. Align front-end interactions with back-end data flows, communications and workflows. Collaborate with Enrollment, Marketing, Information Technology and other departments to improve the prospective student journey. Support integrations among content management, CRM, analytics, personalization and engagement platforms. Document system requirements, data flows, technical processes and operating procedures. Search and Digital Discovery Lead efforts to strengthen organic search visibility and technical SEO performance. Monitor changes in traditional search, AI-assisted search and generative discovery platforms. Optimize website content, structure and technical elements for visibility, retrieval and relevance. Partner with content teams to align search strategy with audience needs and institutional priorities. Establish and monitor search performance standards. Digital Innovation and AI Enablement Evaluate emerging tools that could improve personalization, automation, discovery and engagement. Support thoughtful experimentation with AI-enabled interfaces, workflows and content experiences. Identify opportunities to improve the speed, scale and effectiveness of digital operations. Assess new technologies based on user value, institutional readiness, integration requirements, cost and measurable impact. Help establish responsible and sustainable practices for the use of AI across digital experiences. Collaboration and Project Leadership Work effectively across technical and nontechnical teams to move digital initiatives from concept through implementation. Translate complex systems, requirements and data into clear recommendations. Develop project plans, requirements, documentation and implementation priorities. Coordinate internal stakeholders and external partners when needed. Balance immediate operational needs with the University\u2019s broader digital strategy. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in web design and development, computer science, information systems, management information systems, data analytics, human-computer interaction or a closely related field. Professional experience managing websites, digital platforms or digital products within a complex, user-centered organization. Experience in higher education marketing or enrollment management is preferred. Experience with content management systems, web architecture and web governance. Experience with WordPress is preferred. Demonstrated ability to write, edit and maintain accurate, relevant web content for a variety of audiences. Experience using analytics and behavioral tracking tools to evaluate user behavior, improve digital experiences and measure performance. Experience working within CRM-integrated digital environments. Familiarity with Slate CRM is preferred. Strong understanding of user experience, interface design, accessibility, responsive design and digital quality assurance. Knowledge of conversion optimization, user journey mapping, SEO, AEO, technical search performance and emerging digital discovery practices. Familiarity with HTML, CSS and current front-end web standards is preferred. Experience connecting website activity with CRM, recruitment or enrollment outcomes. Understanding of APIs, system integrations and data pipelines preferred. Familiarity with Python or a similar language used for automation, data analysis or AI-supported workflows is preferred. Experience evaluating or implementing AI-enabled digital tools is preferred. Ability to translate technical concepts, system requirements and data insights for a range of technical and nontechnical audiences. Strong analytical, organizational, documentation, communication and project management skills. Expectations Professional Profile The ideal candidate will be: A systems thinker who understands how platforms, people, processes and data work together. An advocate for intuitive, accessible and user-centered experiences. A strong writer who can make complex information clear and relevant to different audiences. Comfortable working across creative, analytical and technical environments. Curious about emerging technology without losing sight of practical needs and measurable results. Able to balance strategic thinking with hands-on execution. Collaborative, resourceful and committed to continuous improvement. Why Northwood Northwood University is advancing an institutional vision that brings together education, industry and digital innovation. The Digital Experience & Web Strategy Manager will play an important role in shaping how Northwood serves its audiences today and how the University prepares for the future. Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5224630/groundskeeper": {"title": "Groundskeeper", "description": "Groundskeeper Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03450 Division Midland Campus Department Plant Operations Opening Date 04/29/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles The Groundskeeper plays a vital role in preserving and enhancing Northwood University\u2019s award-winning campus, recognized for excellence in beautification and landscape presentation. Spanning over 400 acres, with 70 acres of actively maintained grounds, this position goes beyond routine maintenance to actively support landscape enhancement, design implementation, and long-term environmental stewardship. Through thoughtful planting, horticultural care, hardscape upkeep, and meticulous attention to detail, the Groundskeeper helps sustain the clean, vibrant, and inviting public spaces that distinguish Northwood University. This role directly supports the University\u2019s mission by maintaining safe, welcoming, and aesthetically exceptional outdoor environments for students, employees, and visitors year-round. Responsibilities Perform general grounds operations including but not limited to planting, seeding, weeding, application of herbicides, pruning, trimming, mowing and aeration. Conduct proper watering, fertilizing, herbicide and pesticide applications directed by supervision and incompliance with State of Michigan certification requirements. Operate grounds equipment including tractors, commercial mowers, weed trimmer, power edger, sweeper, snow blower. Perform service, preventative maintenance and repair on all equipment listed above and other auxiliary equipment. Attach and detach plows, power brooms, blades, mower decks and related equipment. Perform snow removal plan including snow blowing, plowing, salting, shoveling and other procedures. Perform additional duties which may be assigned by the Director, the Physical Plant Supervisor or the Maintenance Crew Leader. Assist other maintenance personnel as required. Set up and proper maintenance care of all athletic fields. Be able to operate and repair any of the sprinkler systems in place on campus. Participate in all aspects of campus beautification including, but not limited to: Landscape enhancement (planting, weeding, and maintaining beds) for year-around appeal. Aesthetic maintenance such as removing litter, debris, and graffiti. Horticultural care such as caring for season foliage, shrubs and trees. Hardscape upkeep cleaning of parking lots, sidewalks, parking lots (debris and painting). Maintaining clean, vibrant and inviting public spaces for all to enjoy. Curb appeal, pride and environmental stewardship are key. Qualifications Valid unrestricted Michigan Driver\u2019s License. State of Michigan certification in herbicide and pesticide application. (Within 90 days of hire) Two years\u2019 experience in the horticultural/landscape area or an equivalent combination of the technical training and experience. Successfully pass pre-employment physical. High school diploma or equivalent. Physical Environment: A great deal of physical effort is involved in the following activities: walking, pushing, pulling, climbing and working off ladders, twisting, turning, reaching, squatting bending, kneeling, carrying heavy equipment and supplies weighing up to but not limited to 80 pounds, finger dexterity, visual acuity. A great deal of mental processing is involved in the following areas; reading, remembering, observing and evaluating, reasoning, problem solving, measuring, communicating verbally and in writing, following written and oral directions. Expectations Good written and verbal communication skills. The aptitude for successful completion of the characteristic job duties. Ability to maintain good working relations with supervisors, co-workers and other Northwood University personnel. Promptly report to work, fully ready to work during assigned shift Obtain pesticide license. Be able to work independently without constant direction. Commitment to environmental stewardship. Policy and Procedures: Adhere to all policies and procedures in the Northwood Employee Handbook and all interim policy or procedure put out by Northwood. Must wear all PPE required by Northwood University any deviation can lead to disciplinary action Adhere to all MiOSHA general construction guidelines ABOUT NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5224669/laborer": {"title": "Laborer", "description": "Laborer Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03449 Division Midland Campus Department Plant Operations Opening Date 04/29/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles The General Laborer provides a variety of support services to the University\u2019s groundskeeping, maintenance, and operations teams. This position assists with campus moves, event setups, equipment and supply transport, and basic maintenance tasks. The General Laborer plays an essential role in ensuring smooth daily campus operations and in creating clean, safe, and functional environments for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Responsibilities Campus Moves, Furniture, and Equipment Support Assist with moving furniture, office equipment, and supplies for relocations, remodels, and departmental changes. Install, rearrange, disassemble, and reassemble office furniture as required. Transport materials across campus using carts, dollies, and University vehicles. Organize storage rooms and inventory areas to maintain cleanliness and optimize space. Event Setup and Takedown Set up tables, chairs, staging, outdoor tents, podiums, signs, and other equipment for University events, conferences, ceremonies, and athletic activities. Prepare outdoor areas for campus events, including placing signage, banner installs/takedown, setting up barricades, aligning seating, or assisting with decorations. Remove and store event equipment promptly following events to ensure campus readiness. Grounds and General Maintenance Assistance Assist groundskeepers with routine tasks such as debris pickup, mowing, mulching, raking, and watering. Perform trimming/pruning of trees, bushes and brush. Planting assortment of plants as required. Participate in seasonal work such as leaf collection, snow removal, and ice mitigation. Fix, repair, and adjust all campus sprinkler systems as assigned. Daily pick up of parking lot trash, trash campus wide and trash cans, stone Crete areas as needed. Support maintenance staff with basic tasks including delivering parts, assisting on light repairs, and performing manual labor assignments. Patch blacktop areas. Paint light posts, parking lot painting and repair and other painting as assigned. Assist maintenance technicians with basic building repairs: replacing bulbs, ceiling tiles, air filters, and fixtures. Preventative maintenance procedures include bleacher repair and stadium sealing, fence and post repair, sidewalk and concrete sealing and repair, power washing all brick and cement as needed, roof repairs, gutter cleaning, and drain cleaning of all roofs. Perform minor plumbing and electrical tasks under supervision. Complete basic carpentry projects: shelving installation, trim repair, drywall patching, and painting. Support preventative maintenance by cleaning mechanical rooms, lubricating equipment, and reporting deficiencies. Campus Support and Logistics Perform campus deliveries of supplies, packages, and equipment as directed. Maintain work areas, storage rooms, and equipment in clean and organized condition. Respond to work orders and service requests in a timely and professional manner. Operate University vehicles and equipment safely and responsibly. Other Duties Assist with emergency response efforts, including weather events or urgent facility needs. Support special projects and general operations across Facilities Management. Perform other duties as assigned to ensure the effective functioning of campus facilities and services. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Valid Michigan driver\u2019s license. Strong time-management, problem-solving, and communication skills. Ability to pass a physician-certified health assessment. Physical & Environmental Lift and carry up to 80 pounds regularly. Work in outdoor conditions year-round (heat, cold, rain, snow). Tolerate exposure to chemicals, fertilizers, noise, and dust. Perform tasks requiring standing, walking, kneeling, and bending for extended periods. Expectations Complete assigned tasks within established timelines. Maintain compliance with MiOSHA safety standards and University policies. Demonstrate initiative and accountability when working independently. Uphold professional conduct when interacting with students, faculty, and visitors. Be proficient in operating hand tools and power equipment safely. Use knowledge of horticultural practices and basic building systems. Read diagrams, safety plans, and MSDS sheets. ABOUT NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5479406/new-student-coordinator": {"title": "New Student Coordinator", "description": "New Student Coordinator Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03502 Division Enrollment Management Department UG Admissions Traditional Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles The New Student Coordinator will be responsible for supporting campus events and experiences for incoming students. The New Student Coordinator will plan and execute smaller scale on-campus admissions visits and events (group visits, bus trips, individual campus visits) while supporting the Admissions Events Coordinator with overall event preparation. Additionally, this role will maintain a small recruitment territory. This role will manage invitations, communications, registration forms, and materials, as well as all necessary follow-up for campus events. In addition, this person provides support to the entire admissions team as needed to execute campus events. Responsibilities Achieve new student enrollment objectives for Northwood University in an assigned market channel territory through assigned enrollment activity as established by the Executive Director of Enrollment and Financial Aid. These activities include but are not limited to: develop and maintain consistent referral generation activities visit high school, corporate and professional organizations attend college day/night programs coordinate bus trips to campus participate in on-campus open house events create and host off campus counselor events develop rapport and maintain working relationships with counselors, business teachers, corporation representatives, professional organizations, and related professionals and groups develop presentation materials for target audience and deliver effective presentations actively participate in assisting students from initial inquiry to NU enrollment (manage pipeline) Coordinate and oversee group visits, including high school bus groups visiting campus and offer a robust experience Coordinate and plan itineraries for individual campus visitors, tailoring schedules to the visitors\u2019 unique interests. Organize and communicate visitor itineraries with all individuals included in the schedule, including coaches, faculty, staff, and visitors Brainstorm creative ideas to enhance the visitor experience and better leverage our CRM and other technology Develop communication plan for events including initial invitations and post-event follow up Manage event metrics, tools, surveys, and communication including those in the CRM (Slate) Communicate event details clearly and accurately with admission staff and other campus partners Follow up on all post-event items and keep historical records of event processes Assist admissions counselors by meeting with families individually for daily campus visits Provide weekly activity reports and all necessary documentation in Slate or otherwise required by the director Accurately log and maintain recruitment data in slate in regard to student records and events Evaluate transcripts, if applicable Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree required 1-2 years of event management, preferably in admissions and/or enrollment management Proficiency with CRM required; Slate preferred Excellent oral, written and presentation communication skills Valid driver\u2019s license at time of hire and maintain valid driver\u2019s license while employed; ability to sit in car for prolonged periods of time Ability to travel (intrastate, interstate, regional and/or international where appropriate) Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5410988/northwood-student-recruitment-engagement-coordinator-sri-lanka": {"title": "Northwood Student Recruitment & Engagement Coordinator - Sri Lanka", "description": "Northwood Student Recruitment & Engagement Coordinator - Sri Lanka Location Remote Job Type Non-Employee Job Number 03492 Division International Programs Department International Administration Opening Date 07/15/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood Student Recruitment & Engagement Coordinator Live and Work in Sri Lanka While Representing Northwood University Looking for an international higher education opportunity? Northwood University's longtime international partner, ANC Education in Colombo, Sri Lanka, is seeking a dynamic and globally minded professional to serve as the on-ground representative for Northwood University in Sri Lanka. This is a unique opportunity to live and work in one of South Asia's most vibrant countries while helping students pursue an American university education. This position is employed directly by ANC Education, not Northwood University. Northwood University will assist by promoting the position and conducting an initial review of applicants before qualified candidates are referred to ANC Education for further consideration. Why Consider This Opportunity? Live and work in Colombo, Sri Lanka, a modern coastal city and gateway to one of the world's most culturally rich and beautiful countries. Serve as the primary local representative for Northwood University programs in Sri Lanka. Build relationships with prospective students, schools, businesses, and industry partners. Support students as they begin their educational journey and prepare to continue their studies in the United States. Gain valuable international experience in higher education, recruitment, student engagement, and marketing. About Northwood University Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of: Free Enterprise Ethics Individual Freedom Personal Responsibility Rule of Law Earned Success Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea , Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at its residential campus in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online serves students across multiple states and around the world who seek to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program provides advanced study in leadership and business analytics through a flexible online format. Northwood's international presence includes educational partnerships and International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates, Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about Northwood University at www.northwood.edu . About ANC Education ANC Education is Sri Lanka's leading transnational education provider, offering pathways to American, UK, and Australian university degrees. https://ancedu.com/ For more than two decades, ANC has partnered with Northwood University to deliver undergraduate programs in Business, helping hundreds of Sri Lankan students begin their studies locally before transferring to the United States. Responsibilities Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Recruitment & Marketing Support student recruitment and admissions activities. Develop and implement marketing initiatives to increase awareness of Northwood programs. Represent Northwood at education fairs, school visits, and outreach events. Build relationships with employers and industry partners to create internship and employment opportunities for students. Student Engagement & Success Coordinate onboarding, orientation, and student transition activities. Organize events and engagement initiatives that enhance the student experience. Partner with academic and administrative teams to support student success and retention. Qualifications Ideal Candidate We are looking for individuals who: Hold a bachelor's, master's degree (preferred) in Business Administration, Marketing, Information Technology, Education Management, or a related field. Have experience in higher education, admissions, recruitment, marketing, or student services. Possess exceptional communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Are passionate about international education, student development, and cross-cultural engagement. Are excited about the opportunity to live and work abroad while representing a respected American university. Expectations Employment Information Employer: ANC Education (Sri Lanka) Location: Colombo, Sri Lanka Employment Type: Full-Time Important Notice This position is employed by ANC Education in Sri Lanka and is not a Northwood University employment position. Northwood University is assisting ANC Education by promoting the opportunity and conducting an initial screening of applicants before referral to the hiring institution. Experience the adventure of international living while advancing Northwood University's mission and helping students pursue a world-class American education. Not employed by Northwood University, position is employed by ANC Education in Sri Lanka and benefits will be determined by ANC. Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/3764971/nu-online-adjunct-faculty-distance-education-program-center": {"title": "NU Online Adjunct Faculty, Distance Education Program Center", "description": "NU Online Adjunct Faculty, Distance Education Program Center Location Distance Education Job Type Adjunct Faculty Job Number 03230 Division UG Non-Traditional Program Department UG Non-Traditional Faculty Opening Date 10/16/2022 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University\u2019s NU Online program is now accepting applications for Adjunct Faculty for our Distance Education Program Center to teach courses in the following disciplines: Accounting Automotive Marketing and Management Automotive Aftermarket Management Business Law Computer Science Cybersecurity Data Analytics Digital Marketing Economics Entrepreneurship Environmental Science Finance Health Care Management Hospitality Management History Humanities International Business Management Management Information Systems Marketing Marketing Communications Merchandising & Marketing Mathematics Operations & Supply Chain Management Political Science Speech Sport Management & Esports Management Sustainability Management Click to review Northwood's Course Descriptions. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: A Master's degree in the discipline area from a regionally accredited institution or a Master's degree in a closely related with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the desired discipline. Only applicants who have an understanding of and a commitment to the Northwood Idea need apply. Ability to interact effectively with a wide and diverse range of students and colleagues. Well-developed oral and written communication skills in a variety of delivery formats, especially the format of the class you may be assigned to teach. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in discipline area Certification in Blackboard, Northwood University's Learning Management System (LMS) Availability to teach face-to-face classes Prior teaching experience with adult learners at the college level Five or more years of industry experience in the desired teaching discipline Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. ABOUT NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY Northwood University develops free-enterprise leaders who drive global social and economic progress by promoting the importance of free enterprise, ethics, individual freedom, personal responsibility, rule of law, and earned success. Private, nonprofit, accredited, and guided by The Northwood Idea, Northwood University specializes in managerial and entrepreneurial education at a full-service, residential campus located in Midland, Michigan. Northwood Online is offered in multiple states and online for students with transfer credits and work experience who are looking to complete their undergraduate degree. The DeVos Graduate School of Management offers MBA and Master of Science degrees in Finance, Business Analytics, Human Resources, and Organizational Leadership with day, evening, and online delivery options. The Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) program is delivered online, with a differentiated focus on leadership and business analytics using both qualitative and quantitative methodologies. International education is offered through study abroad and at International Program Centers in Switzerland, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Sri Lanka, Ghana, and France. Learn more about America's Free Enterprise University at www.northwood.edu. Participation in 403b retirement program for eligible employees; sick leave, tuition benefit discounts for eligible employees; access to employee assistance program; wellness benefits; access to other employee discount programs. Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5462838/system-programmer-analyst": {"title": "System Programmer Analyst", "description": "System Programmer Analyst Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03503 Division Finance and Administration Department IT Systems & Programming Opening Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles The System Programmer Analyst, as part of the Systems and Programming Team, is responsible for analyzing business requirements; designing, developing, maintaining, and supporting software applications, integrations, databases, reports, and technical solutions that support University operations. This position works closely with functional departments to identify business needs and develop solutions within Northwood University's Student Information System and related enterprise applications. The System Programmer Analyst serves as a technical resource for software development, systems integration, reporting, database administration, and business process improvement efforts. The position requires independent analysis, problem-solving, and development of solutions that support operational effectiveness and institutional goals. Responsibilities Maintains, enhances, and supports existing application programs, integrations, and reports. Develops new programs, interfaces, APIs, and reporting solutions of varying complexity by utilizing established standards, procedures, and best practices. Analyzes business requirements and translates them into technical solutions. Analyzes data sources, data structures, and business processes to support operational and reporting needs. Designs, develops, tests, and maintains PostgreSQL databases, queries, stored procedures, and related database objects. Develops and maintains API integrations between Ellucian systems, institutional applications, and third-party vendors. Creates and supports web-based applications and interfaces utilizing HTML, XHTML, JavaScript, CSS, and related technologies. Participates in user consultation, systems analysis, system design, and implementation activities. Assists with the development, maintenance, and troubleshooting of Ellucian Insights reports, dashboards, and data models. Assists with the configuration and development of Ellucian Experience cards and related user engagement solutions. Utilizes AI-assisted development and productivity tools, when appropriate, to improve development efficiency, documentation, testing, troubleshooting, and business analysis. Documents application functionality, business processes, database structures, and system integrations. Identifies opportunities to improve business processes through automation, integration, and technology solutions. Recognizes areas where existing policies, procedures, or system functionality require modification or enhancement. Learn and maintain an understanding of university operations necessary to effectively support institutional systems. Collaborates with departments across campus to identify and implement technology solutions. Fulfills departmental requirements related to administrative notification during periods of illness, vacation, or professional development. Performs at or above Information Technology performance standards. Supports systems and processes that span multiple functional areas across the University. Demonstrates excellent customer service, communication, and teamwork skills. Qualifications Possess a bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Management Information Systems (MIS), Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field. Equivalent combinations of education and experience may be considered. Have five or more years of experience in software development, database programming, reporting, systems integration, or related technical work. Demonstrate a strong understanding of application development, system analysis, database concepts, and software engineering principles. Have experience working in Unix/Linux and relational database environments. Demonstrate advanced proficiency in SQL and relational database development. PostgreSQL experience is strongly preferred. Have experience designing, developing, testing, and supporting APIs, web services, and system integrations. Demonstrate strong knowledge of HTML, XHTML, JavaScript, CSS, and modern web development concepts. Possess the ability to perform programming, debugging, system analysis, data analysis, troubleshooting, and problem resolution. Demonstrate experience translating business requirements into effective technical solutions. Have knowledge of software development lifecycle principles, development standards, and best practices. Have experience developing and supporting operational, analytical, and business intelligence reporting solutions. Demonstrate the ability to work independently on complex technical assignments while collaborating effectively with cross-functional teams. Experience with Ellucian Colleague, Ellucian Insights, Ellucian Experience, or other higher education ERP platforms is preferred. Experience utilizing AI-assisted development and productivity tools, including Microsoft Copilot or similar technologies, is preferred. Demonstrate the ability to leverage AI technologies to improve software development, reporting, analysis, documentation, testing, troubleshooting, and operational efficiency while adhering to university security, privacy, and data governance requirements. Possess excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrate strong interpersonal, customer service, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Exhibit the ability to manage multiple projects and priorities simultaneously. Demonstrate initiative, adaptability, and a commitment to continuous learning and professional development. Preferred Technical Competencies Candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas are highly desirable: PostgreSQL database administration and development RESTful API development and integration HTML, XHTML, JavaScript, and CSS development Business intelligence and reporting platforms Ellucian Insights reporting and dashboard development Ellucian Experience card development Data integration and automation technologies AI-assisted development and productivity tools (e.g., Microsoft Copilot or similar solutions) Higher education ERP systems and business processes Cloud-based Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) environments Systems integration architecture and middleware technologies Data governance, data quality, and reporting best practices Expectations Develop, test, debug, and maintain program code. Design and support API-based integrations among institutional systems. Develop and optimize PostgreSQL database solutions and reporting processes. Build and maintain web applications utilizing modern web technologies. Develop, maintain, and support operational and analytical reporting solutions. Assist with the development and support of Ellucian Insights reports and dashboards. Assist with the creation and maintenance of Ellucian Experience cards and user-facing services. Leverage AI-assisted development tools to improve coding efficiency, documentation, testing, troubleshooting, and workflow automation while complying with university data governance and security standards. Document applications, integrations, processes, and code. Troubleshoot and resolve software, reporting, and data-related issues. Assist team members with problem resolution and debugging efforts. Provide excellent customer service and professional support to end users. Demonstrate strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Work effectively both independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Continuously expand technical and functional knowledge of enterprise systems and emerging technologies. Identify opportunities to improve operational effectiveness through automation, integration, reporting, and process improvement initiatives. Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea \u2014 emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood\u2019s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5443447/vice-president-of-finance-and-administration": {"title": "Vice President of Finance and Administration", "description": "Vice President of Finance and Administration Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03497 Division Finance and Administration Department Financial Services and Central Support Opening Date 08/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Vice President, Finance and Administration Shape the Future of a Distinctive University America\u2019s Free-Enterprise University Northwood University seeks an entrepreneurial, strategic, and mission-driven leader to serve as its next Vice President, Finance and Administration . Located in Midland, Michigan, Northwood is a private, nonprofit university founded on the principles of free enterprise, personal responsibility, limited government, and earned success (The Northwood Idea). Since 1959, Northwood has developed graduates who lead organizations, start businesses, strengthen communities, and advance economic opportunity. It is recognized for its fiscal management and leadership in higher education. Today, Northwood is entering an exciting new phase of growth and innovation, marked by its recently adopted 2026-2031 Strategic Plan and the near completion of its $100M comprehensive fundraising campaign. The University seeks an experienced, forward-thinking executive who can help translate strategic priorities into sustainable financial models, drive operational excellence, and ensure long-term institutional success. Reporting directly to the University President and working closely with the Executive Vice-President & COO, the Vice President of Finance & Administration serves as the University's chief financial and business officer and is an essential member of the executive leadership team. The position also serves as Treasurer to the Board of Trustees and plays a central role in aligning institutional resources with mission, strategy, and student success. The Opportunity Northwood University is at a pivotal moment. Known as America\u2019s Free Enterprise University and dedicated to democratic capitalism and the nation\u2019s leading educator for the $2.5 trillion automotive, mobility, and aftermarket industries. No other institution can match its unique position. The university is about to embark on its most substantial capital transformation in its history. This is not a passive role; Northwood is looking for an entrepreneurial, innovative leader to guide \u2014 not just manage \u2014 this next phase, anchored in The Northwood Idea. Leadership Portfolio The Vice President provides executive oversight for a broad portfolio that includes: Finance and Accounting Budgeting and Financial Planning Information Technology Facilities and Capital Projects Auxiliary Services Risk Management and Insurance Compliance and Legal Coordination Strategic Business Operations The successful candidate will bring both strategic vision and operational excellence, balancing innovation with sound financial stewardship. Responsibilities The next Vice President for Finance and Administration will: \u2022 Drive execution of Northwood\u2019s growth-oriented 2026\u20132031 Strategic Plan. \u2022 Build innovative financial and business systems and strategies that fuel enrollment growth and long-term sustainability. \u2022 Align finance, technology, facilities, and administration around institutional priorities. \u2022 Oversee the largest capital infrastructure investment in Northwood\u2019s history, transforming the Midland campus. \u2022 Champion an entrepreneurial culture of creativity, accountability, and results. \u2022 Partner closely with trustees, senior leaders, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. \u2022 Steward one of higher education\u2019s most distinctive missions and philosophies. Qualifications A record of progressively responsible executive leadership in finance, administration, business operations, or related fields is required. Experience in higher education is preferred, though leaders from nonprofit, corporate, or other mission-driven organizations with comparable complexity are encouraged to apply. A CPA credential and advanced degree is highly desirable. Expectations Desired Characteristics Northwood seeks a leader who: Embraces and champions the principles embodied in The Northwood Idea. Possesses exceptional financial and business acumen. Demonstrates integrity, transparency, and sound judgment. Thrives in entrepreneurial and mission-driven environments. Builds trust through collaboration and exceptional communication. Is energized by strategic thinking, problem solving, and continuous improvement. Provides clear, candid counsel to executive leadership. Understands how to align financial strategy with institutional outcomes and growth objectives. About Northwood University Northwood University is unlike any other institution in higher education. For more than six decades, it has advanced a philosophy that champions free enterprise, limited government, ethical leadership, entrepreneurship, and personal responsibility. The University's commitment to innovation, fiscal stewardship, and student success continues to guide its future. Learn more about The Northwood Idea . Qualified candidates selected by the search committee will receive a detailed Leadership Profile outlining the position, strategic opportunities, institutional priorities, and desired leadership attributes. NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply"}}, "rows": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/3764967/adjunct-faculty-various-disciplines-midland-mi": {"school_id": 653, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/3764967/adjunct-faculty-various-disciplines-midland-mi", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Faculty, Various Disciplines, Midland, MI", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "industry experience closely related", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5477986/assistant-professor-accounting": {"school_id": 653, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5477986/assistant-professor-accounting", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor, Accounting", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Accounting", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5138122/assistant-professor-aftermarket-management": {"school_id": 653, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5138122/assistant-professor-aftermarket-management", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor, Aftermarket Management", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Aftermarket Management", "deadline_of_appli